  "notes": "{散財|さんざい} implies spending money somewhat recklessly or extravagantly, but without the negative connotation of {浪費|ろうひ} (waste).\n\nUSAGE:\n- Can be used self-deprecatingly about one's own spending\n- Often used humorously about treating oneself\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {浪費|ろうひ}: waste (more negative)\n- {出費|しゅっぴ}: expense (neutral)\n- {贅沢|ぜいたく}: luxury, extravagance\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {散財|さんざい}する: to splurge\n- {散財|さんざい}させる: to make someone spend money (often said humorously when treating others)",
